ification.json"} {"question" "e-6559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/518a42d25cd993f4bca2498bd9e91a466c7f0c4d71e109b6ab95c9717d34e9e0.png) find $\\,\\overline{\\mathbf{x}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/example-6559.json" "file_sha256" "e199e5cccb13e0ec40b337b79e73f08d0379f5757d94c26d1d1929794a960267" "basis" 1662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-2+5\\text{i} \\\\ 5-9\\text{i} \\\\ -7+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-2+5\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{5-9\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-7+8\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2-5\\text{i} \\\\ 5+9\\text{i} \\\\ -7-8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/example-6559.json" "file_sha256" "e199e5cccb13e0ec40b337b79e73f08d0379f5757d94c26d1d1929794a960267" "basis" 1662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/19d1bb5ad60407748a9c624dee20931c3c70a4bbc3727c4172cfb40384ab6a72.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/f7539ad7301462681681e738b905633b7aa73ca65b5512063e32fa22bcdc0d09.png) are the real and imaginary parts of the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/a7976c73a0aeb9f286a281c193b3a00b38e8bc0fa36a30e985fe1e8f80d7796b.png) what is the value of $ab+cd?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/example-6560.json" "file_sha256" "f8ec08868c2fc7d65d96b7b60fff2dcb4d2079f5890907b31c35aaaf0ca4c704" "basis" 1662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For the given vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/4d6fc79d41790b29a966f7a3303329ab1b778856991ad5b3b85ee3965fce2e33.png) we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+7\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $a=-3, b=5, c=7$ and $d=-2,$ which implies that\n\n$$\nab+cd=(-3) \\cdot 5 + 7 \\cdot (-2) = -29.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/example-6560.json" "file_sha256" "f8ec08868c2fc7d65d96b7b60fff2dcb4d2079f5890907b31c35aaaf0ca4c704" "basis" 1662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\textrm{Im}(k)$ given that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/c51689b9c3a6e7c0e16e5121c725d9400b377ceab8f955bba851c2686991365b.png)\nand\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/1dbce6fee97471e3eb80d3ad5791f70311d6304f7a4d75fac77160e5ad9bee09.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/example-7345.json" "file_sha256" "9bdacf852e90fc6d990eb01fc7d446694c93372c72f166e292506d111d2bc630" "basis" 1662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $\\overline{k\\mathbf{v}} = \\overline{k} \\, \\overline{\\mathbf{v}},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i}\\,\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain that \n\n$$\n4\\textrm{i}\\,\\overline{k}  = 8\\textrm{i}-12\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\overline{k}=\\dfrac{8\\textrm{i}-12}{4\\textrm i} = 2+3\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $k=\\overline{2+3\\textrm{i}}=2-3\\textrm{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\textrm{Im}(k)=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/example-7345.json" "file_sha256" "9bdacf852e90fc6d990eb01fc7d446694c93372c72f166e292506d111d2bc630" "basis" 1662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-77547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vectors ${x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-6\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, then ${x}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb185e10c77846e3e67994b4a553b52c7e497d9a0b2eb82152e51d4b64dad2b3"} {"question" "q-77547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-6\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =\\text{i}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ \\text{i}-2{\\text{i}}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb185e10c77846e3e67994b4a553b52c7e497d9a0b2eb82152e51d4b64dad2b3"} {"question" "q-77547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "62b83643318d1926a8e7351fffa11cfca5b1f16125b0506f4ac9b506dadd7a43"} {"question" "q-77547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb185e10c77846e3e67994b4a553b52c7e497d9a0b2eb82152e51d4b64dad2b3"} {"question" "q-77547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3+8\\text{i} \\\\ -2-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3+8\\text{i} \\\\ 2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3+8\\text{i} \\\\ 2-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3-8\\text{i} \\\\ 2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb185e10c77846e3e67994b4a553b52c7e497d9a0b2eb82152e51d4b64dad2b3"} {"question" "q-77547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb185e10c77846e3e67994b4a553b52c7e497d9a0b2eb82152e51d4b64dad2b3"} {"question" "q-77548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vectors ${x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4+3\\text{i} \\\\ -1+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${x}_{2}=[\\be