ligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=1,b=-1,c=-3$ and $d=-5$, which implies that \n\n$$\nac+bd=1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot (-5)=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb185e10c77846e3e67994b4a553b52c7e497d9a0b2eb82152e51d4b64dad2b3"} {"question" "q-130890" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "62b83643318d1926a8e7351fffa11cfca5b1f16125b0506f4ac9b506dadd7a43"} {"question" "q-130890" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb185e10c77846e3e67994b4a553b52c7e497d9a0b2eb82152e51d4b64dad2b3"} {"question" "q-130890" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb185e10c77846e3e67994b4a553b52c7e497d9a0b2eb82152e51d4b64dad2b3"} {"question" "q-130890" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb185e10c77846e3e67994b4a553b52c7e497d9a0b2eb82152e51d4b64dad2b3"} {"question" "q-76048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,